    "body": "## Why this change is needed\n\nC200's finite static-tray qualification finished, but interrupted publication left GitHub at its preparation checkpoint. This PR publishes the completed implementation and preserved evidence so development can continue from an inspectable result.\n\n## Result and scope\n\nThe explicit `ontokin.static-tray/0.1.0` prototype retains the reviewed exporter logging/action-filter repair. Historical qualification accepted all 12 transactions, with 12 receiving checks, 12 actual-delivery checks, nine corruption variants, and 12 reviewed images. The original C199 failed start and the original coordinator's pending-review result remain intact beside the later independent qualified result. Both native schedules remain closed.\n\nThe candidate preserves all 301 locked input files, 303 original overlay files, 2,565 archive members, and 26 final-review bindings. It adds 74 archived log copies and nine logs recovered from their surviving original paths. Eight recovered stream hashes are new recovery bindings; their weaker historical provenance is explicit.\n\n## Validation and review\n\nFresh CPython 3.12.14/Linux checks passed 107 focused methods, 47 compiler methods, 10 protocol controls, and 43 core cases with 694 assertions. Documentation preservation passed 29 sources and 4,106 local links. No new native, receiving, Node, lifecycle, or author run occurred.\n\nIndependent review approved local candidate `125353836119e50215287c27d80e99cef6d85e8f`, tree `b0e62bdefcb9afd1ea0708ba2b5ab459f457fbcd`. The published tree `7e1ab341160cf5b86807e8ffec2cc3bb7b47db92` adds only five unchanged review artifacts to that reviewed tree; it equals local publication commit `5a7f0b0544684e76a10cdaa88edb09a084eae45e`. Published commit: `0e02d761d70e09fd987cfad1dd85ae8aa1ce679e`.\n\n[Independent review](https://github.com/Omegapy/OntoKin/blob/0e02d761d70e09fd987cfad1dd85ae8aa1ce679e/docs/engineering/static-tray-exporter-c200/evidence/publication-c203/independent-review/REVIEW.md)\n\n## Limits and next gate\n\nThe inherited full regression remains FAILED: 4,239 distinct passing methods and 13 torque-read methods not run after the unchanged 30,000 ms timeout. Shared released runtime, schemas, fixtures, grammar, conformance tools, and workflows are unchanged. Existing visual and compatibility limits remain open. This is experimental integration, with no full-release or comparative-benefit claim.\n\nAfter merge, verify actual main and prepare C201's separate four-export admission protocol. Its coordinator and execution gates remain pending, with zero timed authors.\n\nCloses #136.",
