    "body": "## Owned scope\nOwner `c200-exporter-ef5ae2`, branch `work/c200-exporter-recovery-ef5ae2`, starting from observed main `e8df6496033b13ac7e387c9525fc83c5fada1453`.\n\nRecover C198's self-contained source/history and the later committed C199 failure evidence. Repair the experimental static-tray worker's pinned Blender 4.5.3 exporter logging initialization and inactive action-filter invocation, retaining complete setting coverage and actual startup measurements. Add a separately identified C200 engineering record and independently reviewed frozen qualification revision that explicitly accounts for C199's consumed start.\n\nThe bounded file scope is `prototypes/static_tray_v01/` compatibility/lock coordination where required, focused new controls, and `docs/engineering/static-tray-exporter-c200/`. Historical C198/C199 contracts, locks, ledgers and failed evidence remain immutable. No ordinary compiler, historical tests, limits, tolerances, installed Blender files or hosted-workflow policy change.\n\nNo main integration lease is acquired yet. Parallel source review and packaging work use distinct local branches/worktrees. A verified expected-head main lease is required before eventual reviewed integration or shared STATUS changes.\n\n## Acceptance and recovery\n- Preserve C199 N01's one construction / zero GLBs / zero accepted transactions; never resume or reset its stopped coordinator.\n- Verify the complete pinned exporter execution path, run relevant CPU controls, seal exact source/dependency/command/environment/input bytes, then obtain independent approval before new native work.\n- Execute the separately approved bounded schedule once, stop on first unexpected result, retain failures, and never retry automatically.\n- Preserve 100,000 operations / 30,000 ms ordinary source limits and the 65,000 ms qualification transaction structure.\n- Close with independent result review, guarded integration if eligible, actual-main checks, released ownership, and an offline-restored self-contained next handoff.\n\nDepends on the completed C199 experimental implementation and remains linked to #134. Tray admission and timed author work are separate later gates. The inherited legacy full regression remains FAILED (4,239 passing methods; thirteen torque-read methods NOT RUN).",
